 ## Lifetime
 
@@ -13,8 +12,24 @@ minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 
 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Sessions live in signed cookies, implemented by `sign()` and `verify()` in `larder/sessions.py`. The cookie contains
+URL-safe base64-encoded JSON with the member id (`member`) and an ISO-formatted expiry (`expires`), followed by a dot
+and an HMAC-SHA256 signature. The contents are signed, not encrypted. Verification checks the signature and expiry
+and returns the member id for a valid cookie. A signature mismatch or a past expiry returns `None`.
+
+There is no server-side session store or per-request session query. The old `sessions` table was dropped when the
+cookie implementation shipped; the [decision record](../adr/0002-use-signed-cookies-for-sessions.md) explains why.
+
+## Shared key and logout
+
+All web servers must use the same `LARDER_SESSION_KEY` from deploy secrets. `larder/sessions.py` reads it at module
+import; the code's `dev-only` fallback is for development. Keep the key stable across deploys so existing cookies
+continue to verify on every server.
+
+The server cannot revoke one member's cookie before it expires. Rotating the shared key invalidates everyone's
+existing cookies and logs them out; rotate it only between pickups, as agreed in
+[issue 63](../../notes/issue-63.md). All web servers must load the replacement key.
 
